From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:25:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/30] Costs: allow {T} beside a sacrifice in an {X}
 activation's remaining cost

Lazotep Quarry: "{X}{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Exile target creature
card with mana value X from your graveyard. Create a token that's a copy
of it, except it's a 4/4 black Zombie. Activate only as a sorcery."

CR 107.3 + CR 601.2h + CR 602.2b: after the X mana, the remaining costs
are paid in turn. phase accepted only sacrifice legs in that remainder,
so the {T} leg made the activation "unhandled": offered, then refused
(and a debug_assert panicked in debug builds; casting_costs.rs,
validate_x_mana_sacrifice_residual). Tapping or untapping the source is
paid by the ordinary activation payment once the selected sacrifice is
made, so those legs are now accepted. The Quarry is a Desert too; with
the previous commit it may be the Desert it sacrifices.

Test: tests/integration/lazotep_quarry_x_ability_with_tap.rs. The tests
that expected a {T} leg to be refused now expect it paid
(x_mana_count_plus_tap_taps_after_the_sacrifice) or drop the {T} cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
